Add source editing: GitHub tools, preview links, and publish-by-merge

The agent can now edit page and component source, but never directly. An edit
becomes a branch, a pull request and a Vercel preview deployment; nothing reaches
production until the admin has opened the preview and separately chosen to
publish it.

Tools
- search_site_code, list_site_files, get_site_file (read)
- propose_page_edit (write): exact find/replace against the file's current
  contents, refused if the text is absent or ambiguous
- merge_page_edit: an internal tool with no run and no usable propose, so it is
  unreachable from the agent loop. Publishing is a separate admin click, sent as
  the merge action on an already-applied proposal.

Restrictions live in _shared/github.ts, in one place, rather than being spread
across tools:
- a path denylist covering package.json, lockfiles, vite/tsconfig/vercel/tailwind
  config, index.html, lib/, supabase/, scripts/ and .env
- an extension allowlist: .tsx under pages/ or components/, plus index.css
- one branch per change, never a commit to the default branch
- a size cap, so an oversized file is readable but not rewritable

Commits use the low-level git data API rather than the Contents API, so a
multi-file change lands atomically.

Preview URL resolution uses the Vercel API rather than guessing the generated
hostname, which depends on project naming settings; a wrong guess would send the
owner to a 404 instead of their preview. Without VERCEL_TOKEN the card falls back
to linking the pull request.

The card shows the preview link and a Publish button, and only then merges.
Undo on a source edit closes the pull request and deletes the branch -- nothing
was published, so there is nothing to revert.
